      "content": "Thanks for that. I just ran the draft through the preliminary checker and the rigor score is basically zero. It's way below the threshold for the automated system to even process it for review, so it's just going to get bounced back to my inbox as \"insufficiently documented\" which is going to be a huge pain for the team.\n\nI'm not asking you to change the facts—I need the engineering data to stay exactly as it is—but can you rephrase the log to be a bit more \"rigorous\"? Use those technical terms in the report where they actually make sense for the context. For example, if a system has a certain design, you can mention it. I just need the report to actually get through the compliance filter without being a total lie. Can you try again?",
